<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Shakespeare-light.jpg" alt="A portrait of a ginger cat with blue background." width="450" height="358" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Shakespeare. 8x10, oil on linen. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Last weekend one of the patrons at Upperville Stable Tour asked me if I ever painted portraits of cats.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In truth I paint about 30 dogs for every cat I attempt, although I'm not sure why there is such a great imbalance. After dwelling on this for a few days I decided to try this portrait of Shakespeare. I met him at Willow Hawk Farm, just around the corner from us. He&nbsp;is possibly the friendliest cat that I know.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I used a simple palette of cobalt blue, burnt sienna and yellow ochre over a raw umber block-in. &nbsp;This will be on display and for sale at the Western Loudoun Artists Studio Tour in June. See here for more details: <span style="color: #0000ff;"><a href="http://www.wlast.org" target="_blank">www.wlast.org</a></span></p>